<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="es">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Circuitos Eléctricos - Física</title>
    <style>
        :root {
            --primary-color: #2c3e50;
            --secondary-color: #34495e;
            --accent-color: #2980b9;
            --bg-color: #ffffff;
            --border-color: #bdc3c7;
            --text-color: #333333;
            --font-main: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;
        }

        * {
            box-sizing: border-box;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
        }

        body {
            font-family: var(--font-main);
            color: var(--text-color);
            background-color: #f0f2f5;
            line-height: 1.5;
            -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact; /* Ensure colors print */
            print-color-adjust: exact;
        }

        /* Page Container for Print Simulation */
        .page {
            width: 210mm; /* A4 Width */
            min-height: 297mm; /* A4 Height */
            margin: 20px auto;
            padding: 25mm 15mm; /* Standard margins */
            background-color: var(--bg-color);
            box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
            position: relative;
            overflow: hidden; /* Prevent content spilling out */
        }

        /* Header Section */
        header {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            align-items: baseline;
            margin-bottom: 15px;
            border-bottom: 2px solid var(--primary-color);
            padding-bottom: 10px;
        }

        .brand {
            font-weight: bold;
            letter-spacing: 1px;
            color: var(--primary-color);
            text-transform: uppercase;
            font-size: 0.85rem;
        }

        .meta-info {
            font-size: 0.8rem;
            color: var(--secondary-color);
        }

        h1 {
            font-size: 2rem;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
            color: var(--primary-color);
            font-weight: 600;
        }

        .student-info {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: 1fr 150px;
            gap: 20px;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            font-size: 0.95rem;
        }

        .input-line {
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--text-color);
            height: 1.5em;
            width: 100%;
            display: block;
        }

        .instructions {
            background-color: #f8f9fa;
            padding: 12px;
            border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-color);
            font-size: 0.9rem;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
            color: #444;
        }

        /* Problem Layout */
        .problem-container {
            margin-bottom: 40px;
        }

        .problem-header {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            align-items: center;
            margin-bottom: 15px;
        }

        .problem-title {
            font-size: 1.1rem;
            font-weight: 600;
        }

        .time-tag {
            font-size: 0.8rem;
            color: #7f8c8d;
            font-style: italic;
        }

        .problem-text {
            font-size: 1rem;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            line-height: 1.6;
        }

        /* Diagram Box */
        .diagram-box {
            border: 1px solid #e0e0e0;
            border-radius: 8px;
            padding: 20px;
            background-color: #fff;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
            min-height: 180px;
        }

        /* SVG Styles for Circuit */
        svg {
            max-width: 100%;
            height: auto;
            overflow: visible;
        }

        .wire { stroke: black; stroke-width: 2; fill: none; }
        .component { stroke: black; stroke-width: 2; fill: white; }
        .resistor-body { fill: #e8f6f3; stroke: #16a085; stroke-width: 1.5; }
        .label-text { font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; font-size: 14px; fill: black; font-style: italic; }
        .value-text { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; fill: black; }
        .battery-text { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; fill: black; }

        /* Answer Space */
        .answer-space {
            border-top: 1px dashed #ccc;
            padding-top: 10px;
            min-height: 120px; /* Space for working */
            position: relative;
        }

        .answer-space::after {
            content: "Espacio de respuesta / Procedimiento";
            position: absolute;
            bottom: 5px;
            right: 5px;
            font-size: 0.75rem;
            color: #ddd;
            pointer-events: none;
        }

        /* Print Specifics */
        @media print {
            body {
                background-color: white;
                margin: 0;
                padding: 0;
            }
            .page {
                margin: 0;
                box-shadow: none;
                width: 100%;
                height: auto;
                min-height: auto;
                padding: 15mm 10mm;
            }
            .no-print { display: none; } /* Hide controls if any */

            /* Ensure no page breaks inside problems if possible */
            .problem-container { page-break-inside: avoid; }
        }

        /* Responsive tweaks for screen viewing */
        @media screen and (max-width: 800px) {
            .page {
                width: 100%;
                margin: 10px;
                padding: 15px;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="page">
    <header>
        <div class="brand">AULA VEGA</div>
        <div class="meta-info">Todos los niveles · 5 problemas</div>
    </header>

    <h1>Circuitos eléctricos</h1>

    <div class="student-info">
        <div>Nombre: <span class="input-line"></span></div>
        <div>Fecha: <span class="input-line"></span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="instructions">
        Resuelve cada problema en el espacio indicado. Escribe el procedimiento, no solo el resultado; el proceso es lo que cuenta. Las respuestas están al final.
    </div>

    <!-- Problem 1 -->
    <div class="problem-container">
        <div class="problem-header">
            <div class="problem-title">1. (Media - respuesta numérica con unidad)</div>
            <div class="time-tag">≈ 3 min</div>
        </div>

        <p class="problem-text">
            Dos resistencias <i>R<sub>1</sub> = 25 Ω</i> y <i>R<sub>2</sub> = 50 Ω</i> están conectadas en serie entre los bornes de una batería ideal de 24 V. ¿Qué tensión hay entre los extremos de <i>R<sub>2</sub></i>? (2 cifras significativas)
        </p>

        <div class="diagram-box">
            <!-- SVG Circuit Diagram -->
            <svg width="450" height="160" viewBox="0 0 450 160" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                <!-- Wires -->
                <!-- Left vertical from battery up -->
                <path d="M 60 130 L 60 50" class="wire" />
                <!-- Top horizontal to R1 -->
                <path d="M 60 50 L 140 50" class="wire" />
                <!-- Between R1 and R2 -->
                <path d="M 200 50 L 250 50" class="wire" />
                <!-- After R2 to corner -->
                <path d="M 310 50 L 390 50" class="wire" />
                <!-- Right vertical down -->
                <path d="M 390 50 L 390 130" class="wire" />
                <!-- Bottom horizontal back to battery -->
                <path d="M 390 130 L 60 130" class="wire" />

                <!-- Battery (Left side) -->
                <line x1="45" y1="80" x2="75" y2="80" class="component" stroke-width="3"/> <!-- Long line + -->
                <line x1="52" y1="95" x2="68" y2="95" class="component" stroke-width="3"/> <!-- Short line - -->
                <text x="25" y="92" class="battery-text">24 V</text>

                <!-- Resistor 1 -->
                <rect x="140" y="38" width="60" height="24" rx="4" class="resistor-body" />
                <text x="170" y="30" class="value-text" text-anchor="middle">R₁ = 25 Ω</text>

                <!-- Resistor 2 -->
                <rect x="250" y="38" width="60" height="24" rx="4" class="resistor-body" />
                <text x="280" y="30" class="value-text" text-anchor="middle">R₂ = 50 Ω</text>

                <!-- Current Arrow -->
                <path d="M 220 138 L 240 138" stroke="#c0392b" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#arrowhead)"/>
                <text x="230" y="155" class="label-text" text-anchor="middle" fill="#c0392b">I</text>

                <!-- Definitions -->
                <defs>
                    <marker id="arrowhead" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="7" refX="9" refY="3.5" orient="auto">
                        <polygon points="0 0, 10 3.5, 0 7" fill="#c0392b" />
                    </marker>
                </defs>
            </svg>
        </div>

        <div class="answer-space"></div>
    </div>

    <!-- Problem 2 (Placeholder for layout check) -->
    <div class="problem-container">
        <div class="problem-header">
            <div class="problem-title">2. (Alta - análisis conceptual)</div>
            <div class="time-tag">≈ 5 min</div>
        </div>
        <p class="problem-text">
            En el circuito del problema anterior, si la resistencia <i>R<sub>2</sub></i> se quemara y actuara como un circuito abierto (infinita resistencia), ¿qué pasaría con el valor de la corriente <i>I</i> y la tensión en <i>R<sub>1</sub></i>? Justifica tu respuesta utilizando la Ley de Ohm.
        </p>
        <div class="answer-space" style="min-height: 150px;"></div>
    </div>

</div>

<script>
    // Optional JS to handle simple print trigger if needed, 
    // though standard browser print is preferred for PDF generation.
    window.onload = function() {
        console.log("Worksheet loaded. Ready for print.");
    };
</script>

</body>
</html>
```
